{"step_index":291,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-08T12:26:32Z","content":"If we move **`mtq-mailsrvp-01`** from `inventories/dev/hosts.yml` to **`inventories/prod/hosts.yml`**, here is exactly what changes across networking, automation, safety, and operational governance:\n\n---\n\n### 1. Network & SSH Connectivity: Problem Solved!\n* **The Runner Changes**: Tasks will be routed to the **PROD runner** (**`th2-ansip-run1`** at `172.30.199.225`) instead of the DEV runner.\n* **Firewall Routing**: The PROD runner lives in the datacenter segment that has full routing permission into the Martinique subnet (`172.30.39.0/24`).\n* **Authentication**: The PROD runner injects the key `semaphore-runner-prod`, which is already in `/etc/ssh/authorized_keys/spui-runner`.\n* **Result**: Connection transitions from <span style=\"color:red\">**Operation timed out**</span> to <span style=\"color:green\">**ONLINE (Success)**</span>.\n\n---\n\n### 2. Isolation from Unrelated Production Deployments\nIn [`inventories/prod/hosts.yml`](file:///home/koby/infra-management-system/inventories/prod/hosts.yml), we follow the exact pattern already established for other standalone legacy servers (like `trp-wextp-afe1`):\n\n```yaml\n    # Serveur mail Martinique (Postfix / Dovecot / Roundcube)\n    mtq-mailsrvp-01:\n      ansible_host: 172.30.39.153\n      ansible_port: 30\n      ansible_user: spui-runner\n```\n\n* By defining it under its own dedicated group (`mail_servers`) and **outside** shared groups (`frontaux`, `backends`, `databases`), **standard playbooks will never touch it by accident**.\n* Deployments for web apps, PHP-FPM pools, or MariaDB/ProxySQL will completely ignore `mtq-mailsrvp-01`.\n* It is only targeted when you specifically run a mail playbook or specify `-e target_hosts=mtq-mailsrvp-01`.\n\n---\n\n### 3. Production Governance (\"Règles Dures\") Takes Effect\nBecause it will reside in the PROD inventory:\n1. **Loïc's Explicit Sign-Off**: Any Semaphore task run against the PROD inventory requires explicit confirmation before execution.\n2. **Zero Downtime Guaranteed**: Mail flow (Postfix port 25, Dovecot IMAP/POP3) is strictly protected.\n3. **Reload, Never Restart**: Service configurations are applied via `reload` only.\n4. **Recon Before Modify**: Before any playbook modifies files on `mtq-mailsrvp-01`, a read-only reconnaissance playbook (`recon-*.yml`) must be reviewed first.\n\n---\n\n### 4. Cleaning Up DEV\nWe will remove `mtq-mailsrvp-01` from [`inventories/dev/hosts.yml`](file:///home/koby/infra-management-system/inventories/dev/hosts.yml). This ensures DEV audit playbooks and checks won't fail or wait on 30-second timeouts trying to reach an unreachable Martinique IP.\n\n---\n\n### Summary\nMoving it to `inventories/prod/hosts.yml` aligns the IaC inventory with the **physical network reality** and **host naming** (`mailsrvp` = PROD), allowing the PROD runner to manage it cleanly without any firewall timeouts.","thinking":"**Investigating host inventory details**\n\nThe file describes a legacy front-end host.  This host currently exists outside of current infrastructure-as-code management. It was manually bootstrapped and is inventoried to prepare for future IaC integration.  Noting that it is *not* part of the usual front-end group due to its distinct configuration; specifically, no nginx configuration is pushed to it. There is currently an `ansible_user` missing.\n\n\n"}
